Rāma seizes Paraśurāma's bow and strings arrow --- Rāma spares brāhmaṇa life for Viśvāmitra's sake --- Rāma offers to strike retreat or austerity-won worlds --- Gods with seers gather to watch wonder --- Paraśurāma stands stunned and drained of vigor --- Paraśurāma pleads Kāśyapa exile and claims Mahēndra refuge --- Paraśurāma yields austerity worlds as target and hails Rāma as Viṣṇu --- Rāma looses matchless arrow and destroys worlds --- Gods praise Rāma as quarters clear --- Paraśurāma honors Rāma and departs to Mahēndra